 "kit": "A Longbow Hunter: a bark-brown leather jerkin, worn under a sleeveless surcoat of deep bottle-green cloth that covers his whole chest and belly from the collar down to just below the knees, front and back, split at the front below the belt so the legs can stride and held at the waist by a belt; a deep bottle-green hooded cloak with the hood up, over the shoulders and down the back to the knees with a ragged leaf-cut hem; leather bracers; bark-brown weathered skin; a long yew bow about as tall as the hunter himself, held upright and close to his body; a quiver of grey-fletched arrows on the back; a hunting knife at the belt (in the windup and strike cells the bow is slung on the back and the knife is in hand). No antlers.",
